 of four different stop-gain or frameshift dominant variants","cdna":"","protein":"","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"stop-gain or frameshift","key":"V1"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AD","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["We describe a novel adult onset leukodystrophy in 16 patients from eight families carrying one of four different stop-gain or frameshift dominant variants in the CST3 gene.","The clinical phenotype consists of recurrent episodes of hemiplegic migraine associated with transient unilateral focal deficits and slowly progressing motor symptoms and cognitive decline in mid to older adult ages.","Histopathologic characterization in two autopsy cases did not reveal angiopathy, but instead micro- to macrocystic degeneration of the white matter."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AD","genotype_reason":"single heterozygous variant; mode as stated for the family"},{"id":"R:38729262:1","pmid":"38729262","label":"Chinese patients with adult-onset leukodystrophy","kind":"group","family":"","n_affected":null,"n_families":null,"sex":"","ancestry":"Chinese","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"adult","age_last":"","phenotypes":[{"text":"leukodystrophy","hpo_label":"Leukodystrophy","hpo_id":"HP:0002415","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"CST3","as_reported":"CST3 variants","cdna":"","protein":"","genomic":"","zygosity":"unknown","origin":"unknown","consequence":"","key":"V2"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["Chinese patients with adult onset leukodystrophy caused by CST3 variants."],"quote_grounding":[1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"","genotype_reason":"no genotype or stated mode"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:38489591:1","pmid":"38489591","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Bergner et al. (2024) described pathognomonic MRI changes at typical predilection sites. These involved the deep cerebral white matter, sparing a periventricular and a directly subcortical rim, as well as the middle blade of the corpus callosum, the posterior limb of the internal capsule, the middle cerebellar peduncles, the cerebral peduncles and, specifically, the globus pallidus. The clinical and radiologic features differed markedly from those of Icelandic cerebral amyloid angiopathy caused by the CST3 Leu68Asn substitution.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["Radiologically, pathognomonic changes are found at typical predilection sites involving the deep cerebral white matter sparing a periventricular and directly subcortical rim, the middle blade of corpus callosum, posterior limb of the internal capsule, middle cerebellar peduncles, cerebral peduncles and specifically the globus pallidus.","Clinical and radiological features differ markedly from the previously described Icelandic cerebral amyloid angiopathy found in patients carrying p.Leu68Asn substitution in CST3."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:38489591:2","pmid":"38489591","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Bergner et al. (2024) compared the structures of the CST3 variants and suggested that specific truncations of cystatin C result in abnormal function, possibly by making the protein more prone to aggregation. They stated that this assumed effect remains to be confirmed.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["A structural comparison of the variants in CST3 suggests that specific truncations of cystatin C result in an abnormal function, possibly by rendering the protein more prone to aggregation."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["CST3"],"confirmed":["CST3"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AD"]}